    "content": "# Citation Style\n\n## Books\nAuthor, *Title*, Publisher, Year, p. X / pp. X–Y.\n\n## Journal articles\nAuthor, “Article Title,” *Journal*, volume/issue, year, pages, DOI/URL.\n\n## Manuscripts / archival records\nInstitution, collection/shelfmark, title/description, date, folio/page if available.\n\n## Digital sources\nInstitution/author, title, publication date if available, stable URL/DOI, access date.\n\n## Research rule\nSeparate:\n1. evidence,\n2. source interpretation,\n3. archive's synthesis/conclusion.\n\nDo not convert a traditional genealogy or later ethnonym into a precise ancient date unless the evidence independently supports it.\n"
