    "type": "md",
    "content": "# MASTER RESEARCH INDEX — 2026-10-03\n\n## Preservation rule\nThis index is additive. Existing archive files, source records, folders and research notes must not be deleted or silently rewritten. New research is added with explicit status and provenance.\n\n## Current registry\n- `src/data/kiratWorldSourceCollection.ts`: **45 source/research records**.\n- These 45 are records, not 45 unique people.\n- Current machine audit: 21 `primary_evidence_identified`, 19 `bibliographically_identified`, 6 `page_verification_required` (states may overlap by record semantics; see source audit).\n\n## Today's additional catalogue discoveries\n`TODAY_SEARCH_DISCOVERIES_2026-10-03.csv` records additional British Library catalogue leads found during today's cross-check. These are deliberately **not** counted as confirmed claim-level evidence until individual folios/pages are inspected.\n\n## Evidence chain\n**Claim → Source → Exact page/folio → Actual evidence object → Independent cross-check → Contradiction/uncertainty → Researcher analysis → Final research conclusion → Status/rights/version audit.**\n\n## Core evidence statuses\n- `DOCUMENTED`: directly documented in the identified source/evidence object.\n- `SUPPORTED`: supported by independent sources; still source-bounded.\n- `CHRONICLE_TRADITIONAL`: preserved in chronicles/genealogies/oral traditions, not automatically contemporary proof.\n- `DISPUTED`: credible sources conflict or interpretation is contested.\n- `UNVERIFIED`: source/claim identified but exact evidence not yet checked.\n- `RESEARCH_REQUIRED`: further page/folio/field/archaeological work required.\n- `RIGHTS_RESTRICTED`: evidence object exists but redistribution rights/access are limited or unclear.\n\n## Universal scope\nThe structure is not Kirat-only. The same evidence discipline applies to Nepal, Himalayan, world civilizations, religions, cultures, traditions, oral history, places, inscriptions, archaeology and future archive subjects.\n"
