    "content": "# Published Research Status — 3 October 2026\n\n## Publication snapshot\n\n- **Publication date:** 3 October 2026\n- **Version:** v1.0\n- **Prepared public research records:** 12\n- **Workflow status:** `published`\n- **Research scope:** Current controlled research layer derived from the archive source/claim cross-check registers.\n\n## Professional publication rule\n\nThis publication records the state of research available in the archive **as of 3 October 2026**. It does not represent a claim that every historical proposition in the worldwide literature has been conclusively proven. Each record retains its evidence status, source limitations, disagreements, unresolved questions, rights status, and further-research requirements.\n\nNew primary sources, archival records, oral histories, archaeological evidence, or scholarship can be added through versioned updates without deleting the v1.0 record.\n\n## Publication layers\n\n- Public research synthesis: published.\n- Source and evidence trail: retained in the Research Library.\n- Cross-check/researcher working notes: retained separately from public synthesis.\n- Restricted/copyrighted evidence: represented by citation, catalogue/reference, rights status and official repository link; not redistributed as unrestricted copies.\n- Firestore: remains the authoritative live CMS when the owner imports/publishes the prepared records there. The bundled application contains the same 12 records as the public fallback so the published snapshot is not lost when Firestore has no records yet.\n\n## Count discipline\n\nThe archive currently distinguishes:\n\n- 52 bibliography/hunting-list entries\n- 45 structured source-register records\n- 12 controlled claims\n- 12 prepared published research records\n\nThese are different research layers and must not be represented as 52 or 54 independently verified claims.\n"
