    "content": "# Today's Cross-Check Log — 2026-10-03\n\n## A. Archival catalogue discoveries\nBritish Library EAP1023/21 and EAP1023/22 catalogue records expose additional Kiranta/Kiranti manuscript objects. They are recorded as **catalogue evidence objects/leads**, not as automatically verified historical claims.\n\n### EAP1023/21 (Lakshman Banstola Collection)\n- EAP1023/21/5 — `किराँत धर्म / Kiranta Religious book` — 16th-century catalogue date; 21 paper folios; 21 TIFF images; research-only access and not-public-record legal status.\n- EAP1023/21/6 — `किरांत कथा / Kiranta Story` — 16th-century catalogue date; 30 folios; 32 TIFF images.\n- EAP1023/21/7 — `किराँत पुस्तक / Kiranta Book` — 15th-century catalogue date; 9 folios; 12 TIFF images; described as a book of Kiranta religious culture.\n- EAP1023/21/8 — `नेपालराज बंशावली / Nepalraj Vamshavali` — 18th-century catalogue date; 18 folios; 22 TIFF images; described as a Nepal chronicle mentioning ruling kings.\n- EAP1023/21/9 — `किराँत प्रार्थना / Kiranta Prayer` — 15th-century catalogue date; 10 folios; 11 TIFF images; Kiranti language and Sirijangha script.\n- EAP1023/21/10 — `किराँत प्रार्थना / Kiranta Prayer` — 15th-century catalogue date; 1 folio; 9 TIFF images.\n\n### EAP1023/22 (Hareram Upadhyaya Collection)\n- EAP1023/22/3 — `किराँत दस्ताबेज / Kirata Dastabej` — 16th-century catalogue date; 8 folios; 8 TIFF images; catalogue says recovered from a Kiranta society in Eastern Nepal.\n- EAP1023/22/16 — `किराँत देवदेवी कथा / Story of Kiranta Gods` — 16th-century catalogue date; 3 folios; 3 TIFF images; Kiranti language and Sirijangha script.\n- EAP1023/22/17 — `किराँत धर्म / Kiranta Book of Religion` — 16th-century catalogue date; 25 folios; 27 TIFF images.\n- EAP1023/22/18 — `किराँत प्रार्थना / Kiranta Prayer` — 16th-century catalogue listing.\n- EAP1023/22/19 — `किराँत प्रार्थना / Kiranta Prayer` — 16th-century catalogue listing.\n- EAP1023/22/20 — `किराँत प्राथमिक पुस्तक / Kiranta Primary Book` — 16th-century catalogue listing.\n- EAP1023/22/21 — `किराँत ज्योतिष / Kiranta Jyotisha` — 16th-century catalogue listing.\n\n## B. Cross-check interpretation\nThese records establish that the catalogue contains specific Kiranta/Kiranti manuscript objects. They do **not by themselves establish** the historical truth of every statement that may appear inside those objects. Each claim must be tied to the exact folio/text and then cross-checked with independent evidence.\n\n## C. Existing major evidence already retained\n- Hamilton 1819: direct documentary evidence for Kirat/Kichak in eastern Nepal in the early 19th century; exact page targets already recorded.\n- Documenta Nepalica: Pallo Kirāta corpus and RRC_0036_0252 appeal document.\n- Hodgson papers: Limbu/Kiranti language, religion, culture, genealogy and manuscript holdings.\n- Yalambar/Yellung: chronicle/traditional-historical status; exact ancient reign and Mahabharata identity remain unresolved.\n\n## D. Negative controls\nNo page, folio, quotation, date, identity equivalence or “100% proof” is added unless the source itself supports it and the evidence object has been checked.\n"
