    "content": "# Kirat / Kiranti Cross-Check Matrix — 2026-10-03\n\n## Rule\nEvery record separates **source statement → evidence object → independent cross-check → researcher analysis → final conclusion**.\n\n| Topic | Cross-check result | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Eastern Kirat/Kichak population in early 19th c. | Hamilton pp. 7–8 is primary written evidence; his named informants and later archival/ethnographic sources provide additional context. | DOCUMENTED, SOURCE-BOUNDED |\n| Agam Singha as hereditary Kirat chief/informant | Hamilton identifies him on pp. 2–3 and refers to his account again on pp. 133–134. | DOCUMENTED IN HAMILTON |\n| Yellung/Yalamba/Yalambar as first Kirata ruler | Repeated in chronicle-based historical scholarship, including Ancient Nepal and later compilations. | CHRONICLE/TRADITIONAL-HISTORICAL |\n| Yalambar = a specific Mahabharata character | No independent contemporary evidence established in this pass. | NOT ESTABLISHED |\n| 16th-century Kirant religious manuscripts | British Library catalogue records digitised manuscript objects and their image counts. | DOCUMENTED OBJECT / RIGHTS RESTRICTED |\n| Limbu religion/culture manuscripts in Hodgson papers | British Library confirms holdings on religion, culture, worship, ritual, customs and vocabulary. | DOCUMENTED ARCHIVAL HOLDING |\n| Mundhum as oral religious/cultural tradition | TU academic research describes Mundhum as oral religious/narrative tradition; claims remain attributed to the specific research/community context. | SECONDARY SCHOLARLY EVIDENCE |\n\n## Negative controls\n- “Chronicle says” ≠ “contemporary history proves”.\n- “Digitised” ≠ “free to redistribute”.\n- Variant name ≠ proven identity equivalence.\n- One modern thesis ≠ proof of an ancient claim.\n- Missing page/folio numbers are never filled from memory.\n\n| Pallo Kirāta administrative records | Documenta Nepalica catalogue lists multiple reliable records dated 1780–1851 and related years | Strong primary-document catalogue evidence; individual folios still require page-level inspection | DOCUMENTED ARCHIVAL CORPUS |\n| VS 1865 appeal to Kirātīs/Lepchas | RRC_0036_0252, 2 folios, RRC vol.36 no.221, NGMPP E 2441/2 | Concrete archival document; do not generalize beyond its actual text | PRIMARY DOCUMENT IDENTIFIED |\n| Government Kirant dynasty narrative | Nepal Parichaya p.46 | Useful official compilation; must be cross-checked against the underlying Vamsavali/chronicle sources | SECONDARY/OFFICIAL COMPILATION |\n"
