    "title": "YALAMBAR CROSS CHECK STATUS 2026 10 03",
    "type": "md",
    "content": "# Yalambar / Yellung / Ya’lamba — Cross-Check Status — 2026-10-03\n\n## Current evidence position\n1. Yellung/Ya’lamba/Yalambar is preserved in Nepalese chronicle-based historical traditions as an early/founding Kirata ruler.\n2. Government `Nepal Parichaya` p.46 also presents a Yalung/Yalambar narrative, but it is an official compilation and must be cross-checked against its underlying chronicles.\n3. Early nineteenth-century Hamilton provides independent documentary evidence for Kirat/Kichak communities in eastern Nepal, but **Hamilton is not direct evidence for Yalambar**.\n4. The exact historical date/reign of Yalambar is not established by the contemporary documentary evidence identified in this pass.\n5. Identification of Yalambar with a specific Mahabharata character is **not established** by the evidence currently recorded here.\n6. “Hang = Yalambar’s verified ancient official title” remains **not established** unless a source directly supports it.\n\n## Required negative controls\n- Chronicle statement ≠ contemporary proof.\n- Variant names ≠ proven identity equivalence.\n- A later government compilation ≠ independent ancient evidence.\n- A catalogue date ≠ automatically a securely established manuscript composition date; preserve the catalogue wording.\n"
