    "title": "YALAMBAR FINAL RESEARCH STATUS 2026 10 03",
    "type": "md",
    "content": "# Yalambar — Final Research Status (2026-10-03)\n\n## Current conclusion\nAvailable evidence supports the conclusion that Yellung/Ya’lamba/Yalambar is preserved in Nepalese chronicle traditions as the founder or first ruler of the Kirata dynasty. Historical documentary evidence independently supports the existence of Kirat/Kichak communities in eastern Nepal in the early nineteenth century.\n\nThe exact date of Yalambar's reign, the precise historical identity represented by variant name forms, the identification of Yalambar with a specific Mahabharata character, and the claim that “Hang” is a securely established ancient official title are **not conclusively established by the contemporary evidence identified in this research pass**. These remain chronicle/traditional-historical or unresolved claims unless stronger primary evidence is identified.\n\n## Negative controls\n- Chronicle tradition is not automatically contemporary proof.\n- A name variant is not automatically identity equivalence.\n- A Mahabharata association is not automatically historical identification.\n- Missing page/folio evidence is never filled from memory.\n"
