    "path": "04_ORAL_HISTORY_AND_FIELD_RESEARCH/FIELDWORK_INDEX/MASTER_FIELD_CROSS_CHECK_QUESTION_MATRIX_2026-10-03.md",
    "title": "MASTER FIELD CROSS CHECK QUESTION MATRIX 2026 10 03",
    "type": "md",
    "content": "# MASTER FIELD CROSS-CHECK QUESTION MATRIX\n## For continuation after current documentary/source audit\n\n### Rule\nField research must test specific existing claims. It must not be used to manufacture agreement with books. Every answer is stored as testimony with informant attribution.\n\n| Field topic | Existing evidence to test | Questions for elders/knowledge holders | Evidence to record |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Yalambar/Yellung/Ya'lamba | Chronicle/traditional accounts | What name is used locally? Who taught this story? How many generations? What place is associated with it? Are there different versions? | Video/audio, transcript, place photos, informant details |\n| Kirat settlement | Hamilton early-19th-century account | Which ancestors are said to have settled here? From where? Which old place names survive? | Video, genealogy, place-name map/photo |\n| Kirat/Kiranti group names | Hodgson and later scholarship | What self-name/ethnonym is used? What names are used by neighboring groups? | Recorded terminology, pronunciation, context |\n| Mundhum | Academic and oral-tradition sources | Who performs/recites it? On what occasions? Who taught it? What variants exist? | Full/approved recording, transcript, performer details |\n| Genealogy | Chemjong/Tanka Rai/local genealogies | Which ancestors are remembered? What written/oral genealogy exists? Where did the record come from? | Genealogy scan/photo, interview, independent informant |\n| Old documents | Documenta Nepalica / local records | Does the family/community possess old land, tax, royal, ritual or genealogical documents? | Owner-approved photos/scans, metadata, rights |\n| Place history | Historical maps/documents | What was this place called before? What structures/settlements existed? | GPS/place description, photos/video, oral accounts |\n| Religious practice | British Library/Hodgson and scholarship | Which practices are remembered? What has changed? Which terms are old/local? | Ritual testimony, permitted photos/video, consent |\n| Administrative history | Pallo/Majha Kirāta records | What old offices, taxes, land/custom terms are remembered? | Interview + local documents + comparison |\n\n### Minimum informant record\n- Full name or approved public name\n- Approximate/actual age if consented\n- Community/role\n- Village/locality\n- Ancestral locality\n- Interview date/time/place\n- Interviewer\n- Camera/audio operator\n- Consent for recording\n- Consent for public archive or restricted use\n- Language/dialect\n- Relationship to the tradition\n- How the informant learned the information\n\n### Cross-check rule\nFor significant historical claims, seek more than one independent informant where feasible. Record agreement and disagreement explicitly. Do not delete contradictory testimony.\n"
